# §2026-02-14 — .env / credentials files MUST be committed to repo for
# Emergent's Kubernetes deployment to pick up env vars on Redeploy.
# Do NOT add back to .gitignore. Production was running OLD code for
# 24h because .env was blocked from reaching the GitHub repo on
# "Save to GitHub". Secret rotation is handled via the Emergent
# Deploy panel's Environment Variables section, not via .gitignore.
frontend/node_modules/.cache/default-development/1.pack
frontend/node_modules/.cache/default-development/5.pack
frontend/node_modules/.cache/default-development/0.pack
frontend/node_modules/.cache/default-development/3.pack
frontend/node_modules/.cache/default-development/4.pack
-e 
# §2026-02-15 — .env files were re-added by some auto-tool. Per founder
# directive (iter 82 + iter 85), .env files MUST stay tracked so
# Emergent's Save-to-GitHub flow ships them to production. Production
# was running OLD env vars for 24h+ when this block existed. Do NOT
# re-add `.env`, `.env.*`, or `*.env` to this file under any
# circumstance. Secret rotation belongs in the Emergent Deploy panel,
# not in .gitignore.
credentials.json
*.pem
*.key
.credentials
frontend/node_modules/.cache/default-development/7.pack
-e 
